im  for revenge and that champ was none  other than black adam who went on to  free the seven deadly sins based on this  light show and the clips we've seen it's  looking like dceu's black adam was  inspired by black adam's new 52 origin  story that debuted in 2011's justice  league volume 2 run in the comics adam  and his nephew aman were slaves in  kondok thousands of years ago after the  rest of their family is murdered by  dictators the wizard blesses both adam  and aman with his powers hoping that  these two new champions use them to save  kondok with his heartful of revenge adam  kills his nephew steals his power and  rules over conduct with an iron fist  he's imprisoned by the wizard for his  betrayal and awoken 5 000 years later  swearing vengeance on shazam from dc's  2021 fandom teaser we know that this  movie will show black adam duking it out  with the wizard before being sealed away  in ruins within conduct side quest while  we're talking about that fandom teaser  the opening image of kondok is pulled  directly from 2016's 52 issue number one  those statues looked so cool in the  comics and i'm stoked that we get to see  this view recreated for the big screen  from another previous trailer we learned  that adam's son sacrificed his life to  save his father here in the teaser we  see his son raise his arms in an  offering before being killed while adam  watches powerless to save him this  reminds me of 1999's justice society of  america number 43 and 44 in which black  adam reveals to shazam that his wife and  son were killed in conduct by the  powerful priest octon driving him to  seek revenge i predict that this movie  will expand on the premises introduced  in both justice league volume 2 and just  as society of america showing the pain  suffering and desire for vengeance that  drove black adam in the aftermath of his  family's deaths black adam's voiceover  tells us that his powers are not a gift  but a curse born out of rage black adam  likely views his abilities in this light  because his near immortal status  prevents him from dying and finding  peace from his survivor's guilt next we  see a brand new look at black adam's  suit lit up by streams of lightning  illuminating his eyes radiating from the  bolt on his chest and making him look  badass as i'll get out again i got a  throw to this image from 2011's justice  league vol 2 issue 10 and 2013 shazam it  was clearly the inspiration for this  exact moment down to the glowing eyes  now is it just me or does the blue  energy of this look like the rpg missile  from the first trailer if you look  closely at the rocket the rock is rocket  blocking there's a glowing blue light  inside the chamber when it explodes it  emits a light blue wave of smoky light  that looks like a smaller version of  this gigantic explosion in this teaser  this tells me that the teaser's  explosion was likely set off by the  organization sent to free black adam the  antagonistic inter-gang in the comics  intergang is an organized crime  syndicate supplied with weapons from the  evil new gods of apocalypse seeing the  power level of their current weaponry  makes me wonder if they've already been  messing with otherworldly tech possibly  repurposing an assortment of scavenged  resources from previous dceu entries  this explains how they could have the  hoverbikes seen later in the trailer as  well i love dr fate's intro in this  teaser he phases into the room in static  golden light that dissipates as he  removes the helmet of fate it's pierce  brosnan you gotta take off the helmet  and look at that gorgeous face according  to the comics the helmet of fate is one  of the most powerful artifacts in the dc  universe and grants the user a butt ton  of powers like spell casting healing  flight and elemental manipulation to  name a few as he touches the top of it  later on a red zap of light appears  beneath his hand seemingly  telepathically alerting him to some sort  of cosmic disturbance possibly the  awakening of black adam when we see fate  fight black adam later on in the trailer  he uses a sorcery to create several  copies of himself just like his marvel  counterpart dr strange the cloak he's  wearing is the cloak of destiny an  artifact that's resistant to both fire  and magic he presents black adam with  two choices he can either save the world  or destroy it but as an anti-hero this  dude doesn't operate in black and white  good and evil he's not a hero or a  villain he's black adam still we've got  to acknowledge that the justice society  of america's talent scouts are seeking  to put ba on a redemption arc the next  time we see dr fate and the teaser  notice the jet flying overhead this is  the justice society of america's steel  eagle aka the personal aircraft flown by  the jsa a few moments later a maskless  atom smasher played by noah centineo  sits inside with fate and hawkman just  before the jet crashes into the side of  a building in conduct causing an  explosion that destroys an open-air  market next we see the swirling blend of  red hair and green robes that is cyclone  lead by quintesses swindell who uses her  wind manipulation powers to throw a  bunch of pipes at black adam to capture  him just like in the comics her  character will be a part of the jsa in  the film then we see adriana tomez  played by actor sarah shai who said in  an interview that her character is quote  a freedom fighter that's leading this  big resistance against an evil malicious  group called intergang in the comics  intergang kidnaps adriana and gives her  as a gift to black adam who thankfully  is like bro women aren't gifts adam  bestows upon her the amulet of a seat  and she's imbued with the powers of  superhuman speed and durability light  healing elemental manipulation and  telekinesis when hawkman played by  aldous hodge leaps skyward wings  unfurled you can see a kfc in the  background here it stands for kendaki  fried chicken finger licking good  embarrassingly for hawkman his  thanagarian mace and low wingies are no  match for black adam's lightning that  mace is made out of the same material  that gives hawkman his powers nth metal  an alien metal that negates gravity you  know black adam is strong if he can just  grab onto that thing like a baby rattle  with all of the uncertainties and  variables floating around in the dceu my  hope is that black adam will help to  revitalize these movies steering them in  a direction that us fans will appreciate  it's like dwayne johnson himself once  said the rock is basically franchise  viagra  franchise viagra so if anyone can catch  dc fans attention with black adam it's  this guy follow me on instagram and  twitter whitneypuppy follow new rockstar  subscribe to new rockstars for more  analysis of everything you love and  thanks for watching bye  [Music]  you

